00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,000
No plan. No backup. No choice.

2
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Mission: Impossible - Ghost Protocol is a action,
thriller, adventure film directed by Brad Bird.

3
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Ethan Hunt and his team are racing against time to track down a dangerous terrorist named Hendricks, who has
gained access to Russian nuclear launch codes and is planning a strike on the United States.

4
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
An attempt to stop him ends in an explosion causing severe destruction to the Kremlin and the
IMF to be implicated in the bombing, forcing the President to disavow them.

5
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,000
No longer being aided by the government, Ethan and his team chase Hendricks around
the globe, although they might still be too late to stop a disaster.

6
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Ethan Hunt, played by Tom Cruise.

7
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Jane, played by Paula Patton.

8
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Benji, played by Simon Pegg.

9
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Brandt, played by Jeremy Renner.

10
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Hendricks, played by Michael Nyqvist.

11
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:21,000
Sidorov, played by Vladimir Mashkov.

12
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Mission: Impossible – Ghost Protocol is a 2011 American action spy film directed by Brad Bird (in his live-action directorial
debut) from a screenplay by the writing team of Josh Appelbaum and André Nemec, who also serve as co-producers.

13
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
Produced by Tom Cruise, J.

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
Abrams, and Bryan Burk, it is the sequel to Mission: Impossible III (2006) and
the fourth installment in the Mission: Impossible film series.

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
The film stars Cruise, Jeremy Renner, Simon Pegg, and Paula Patton, with Michael Nyqvist,
Vladimir Mashkov, Josh Holloway, Anil Kapoor, and Léa Seydoux in supporting roles.

16
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
In the film, the Impossible Missions Force (IMF) is shut down after being publicly implicated in a bombing of the Kremlin, causing Ethan
Hunt (Cruise) and his team to go without their usual resources or backup in a life-threatening effort to clear their names.

17
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
Development for Mission: Impossible – Ghost Protocol began in August 2009, when Appelbaum and Nemec were hired to write
the screenplay (which was later rewritten by eventual series director and writer Christopher McQuarrie).

18
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
Cruise's return was confirmed by March 2010 after Bird was announced to direct the film,
replacing Abrams (who directed the predecessor), who stayed on this film as a producer.

19
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:21,000
The film was officially titled in October 2010, after which, principal photography took place and lasted until March 2011, with filming
locations including Bangalore, Mumbai, Budapest, Moscow, Dubai, and Canadian Motion Picture Park Studios in Vancouver.

20
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
Like previous entries in the franchise, the cast, most notably Cruise, completed
most of their own stunts, while parts of the film were shot in IMAX.

21
01:39:45,000 --> 01:39:51,000
Mission: Impossible – Ghost Protocol premiered at the Dubai International Film Festival on December 7, 2011, and was released in IMAX and select
large-format theaters on December 16, before being theatrically released in the United States by Paramount Pictures on December 21.

22
01:44:30,000 --> 01:44:36,000
It received positive reviews from critics, with praise for the action
sequences, Cruise's performance, and Bird's direction.

23
01:49:15,000 --> 01:49:21,000
It grossed $694.7 million worldwide, becoming the fifth-highest-grossing film of 2011, as well as the highest-grossing film in the
franchise and the highest-grossing film starring Cruise until it was surpassed by Mission: Impossible – Fallout (2018).

24
01:54:00,000 --> 01:54:06,000
Retrospective reviews later credit the film for revitalizing the
Mission: Impossible franchise back into mainstream success.

25
01:58:45,000 --> 01:58:51,000
The film was followed by Mission: Impossible – Rogue Nation in 2015.

26
02:03:30,000 --> 02:03:36,000
The film explores themes of mask, assassin, budapest,
hungary, skyscraper, secret intelligence service.

27
02:08:15,000 --> 02:08:21,000
The tone is intense.
